  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, status indicators overlap icons, partially obscuring them. An icon is, quite literally, a symbol, and I believe nothing should be allowed to cover it up.\n\nThe same applies to group banners. They may represent something a user stands for, or they may simply serve a decorative purpose. Either way, covering them with Trust Rank or Avatar Rank indicators is not a sensible design choice. Especially when there’s a huge amount of empty space directly below them, is there really any need to deliberately obscure group banners? (No, there isn’t.)\n\nBoth icons and group banners allow users to upload images of their choice. In the worst-case scenario, this freedom, combined with overlapping UI elements, can result in an absolutely terrible UI/UX experience for both the general public and users with visual impairments.\n\nI urge you to address this issue as soon as possible.",
